WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.305
A star letting go.

00:01.983 --> 00:04.072
A star like the Sun does not explode.

00:04.496 --> 00:09.520
Late in its life it blows its outer layers away into space, and they glow like this.

00:10.054 --> 00:13.959
This is the Helix Nebula, six hundred and fifty light-years away.

00:14.558 --> 00:19.353
The small, very hot star at its centre is all that is left: a white dwarf.
